<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sydney, Nova Scotia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney">Sydney</a> is the main town of Cape Breton Island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>. It was founded in 1785 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-frederick-wallet-desbarres">Joseph Frederick Wallet DesBarres</a> as the capital of the separate colony of Cape Breton, which was merged into Nova Scotia in 1820. Nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> mines and, from the early 1900s, a large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> plant made it an industrial centre until their decline in the late 20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sydney-nova-scotia.jpg" alt="Sydney, Nova Scotia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Quintin Soloviev · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sydney,_Nova_Scotia_skyline.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
